			</key>
			<key>
				<name>MMB</name>
				<desc>adjust power lever (middle mouse button)</desc>
			</key>
			<key>
				<name>M/m</name>
				<desc>Raise or lower the winch</desc>
			</key>
			 <key>
        <name>q</name>
        <desc>Rotate Searchlight Up</desc>
      </key>
      <key>
        <name>a</name>
        <desc>Rotate Searchlight Left</desc>
      </key>
      <key>
        <name>z</name>
        <desc>Rotate Searchlight Down</desc>
      </key>
      <key>
        <name>d</name>
        <desc>Rotate Searchlight Right</desc>
      </key>
<line>All external lights are default to OFF. Light switches are located on the central switch panel </line>
			<line> </line>
			<line> Rotorbrake can only be activated from the lever on the overhead panel</line>
			<line>Winch man is only available on configurations containing the side winch and when the sliding door is open </line>
		<line> </line>
		<line>Emergency Flotation system. </line>
		<line>The Floatation system is selectable from rhe the Equipment - Fuel + payload menu </line>
		<line>Once equipped with the floatation system, the "Float Arm" button on the central switch panel will become active. Press this to ARM the system. </line>
		<line>You should also see a red handle  on the right of the Centre console, this is the Deploy handle. Click that to deploy the floats ( yes you can float on water ) </line>
		<line>The floats can be repacked and the system reset by clicking the deploy handle again while on the ground. </line>
		<line> </line>
		<line> AS350 B3+ Manual start proceedure.</line>
		<line>PREPARATION</line>
		<line> Rotorbrake...forward / released</line>
		<line> Fuel shut-off lever ... forward and secured </line>
		<line>Twist grip...Idle position ( power to 63%) </line>
		<line>Battery..ON  </line>
		<line>Gen...  OFF </line>
		<line> Horn ON ( optional )</line>
		<line>Avionic ON </line>
		<line>Gyro ON </line>
		<line>Instrument light ...as required ( default OFF )</line>
		<line> Warning lights (W/LT TST)...Press to test </line>
		<line>Warning panel lights should be :- GENE, FUEL P, PITOT, HORN, HYDR, ENGP, MGB P, TWT GRP, BATT</line>
		<line> </line>
		<line>ENGINE START</line>
		<line>CPW... check GOV light is OFF </line>
		<line>Fuel pump.... ON (FUEL P light should be off )</line>
		<line>GENE ... OFF ( GENE warning light should be off )</line>
		<line>Starter Selector... ON ( CRANK button on the Switch panel of a B3+)</line>
		<line>Check parameters : Ng... increase   TOT ...below limits   Engine oil pressure ....checked </line>
		<line>N1 = 10% disengage starter. </line>
		<line>When N1 > 63% you are art idle</line>
		<line>Whwn N1= 63%, GENE- ON, BATTERy-OFF</line>
		<line>Warning lights... all out, exc. HORN / PITOT / TWT GRIP /GENE</line>
		<line> Pitot.... ON </line>
		<line>Fuel Pump ... OFF </line>
		<line> Twist grip.... flight position ( power to 100%)</line>
		<line> Fire Test - press to test on main switch panel</line>
        <line> External lights as required ( default is OFF )</line>
		<line></line>
<line> SAR Menu option - THIS IS JUST A FUN MULTIPLAYER FEATURE !!</line>
			<line> If you crash your chopper, you can use this menu option to call on another AS350</line>
			<line>or any other chopper running the script, to retrieve your broken chopper and you, as an underslung load.</line>
<line> </line>
<line>AUTOPILOT V3 </line>
<line>The Autopilot is now able to control  speed, altitude and heading. Autopilot is only usable  between 30-140kts</line>
<line>Heading modes can be used without any other Autopilot function being active.</line>
<line>Speed modes can be used without any other Autopilot function being active.</line>
<line>****  Altitude modes can only be used in conjunction with speed mode being being active. This includes the use of Vertical Speed mode.  ***</line>
<line>AUTOPILOT ISSUES !!!!!</line>
<line>When disengaging the AP entirely or from a singe mode, the  control inputs will snap to your actual cyclic/colective/pedal positions as soon as you  move any of them.</line>
<line>This is unavoidable as  the sim can not physically move your cyclic/colective/pedal positions to match the Autopilots input.</line>
<line>The best advice to minimise the sudden change of input would be for you to  have your cyclic/colective/pedal positions ready in approximatly correct positions  to minimise the "snap".</line>

		</help>
